# patching-hosts host knob (#77). Grammar: the vendored skill's
# references/knob.md. The skill reads this file and never writes it.
# Times are UTC. A malformed line makes the host report-only until fixed.

class production
posture scheduled

# --- when -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The owner's monthly window: Monday 23:00 to Tuesday 05:00, the broker's
# hours (CannObserv/broker#67), on a different Monday from the broker's run so
# a bus flap stays attributable to one host. Every step's whole span must fit
# inside it, or apply.sh refuses it.
window Mon 23:00-05:00

# No quiet line. processor-drift.timer is OnUnitActiveSec=1h, AccuracySec=1min:
# its ticks drift, so no fixed range fits, and a tick is a GitHub API read
# and a Status check-in. Liveness checks in every 5 min from inside
# `processor run`; a stop past its 900 s grace pages (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).

# --- the service ----------------------------------------------------------
# Stopped in the reboot chain, and checked after boot for its first start and
# NRestarts. KillMode=mixed + TimeoutStopSec=240 let the in-flight command
# finish; one cut off stays pending and is reclaimed (store -> publish -> ack).
# A deploy restarts it outside any window, by the owner's choice (2026-10-26):
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md § Patching.
service processor.service

# An extraction mid-run: its child is a `python -I -m processor._child`.
# Visible to a non-root pgrep (/proc has no hidepid). The chain re-checks it.
inflight pgrep -c -u processor -f 'processor\._child' || true

# --- checks (never root: they run as the invoking user, exedev, in adm) ---
health systemctl is-active --quiet processor.service
# Nothing at WARNING or above in 6 min: a backoff, a failed check-in, a stale
# loop, or systemd's own warning lines for the unit. Valid only after #76's
# deploy, 2026-10-25T15:50:36Z (journald PRIORITY follows the record's level).
health test "$(journalctl -u processor -p warning --since -6min -q -o cat --no-pager | wc -l)" -eq 0

# --- third-party apt origins ----------------------------------------------
# NodeSource: agent tooling only, follow (#6; scoped by deploy/apt/nodesource.pref).
# Named by its site: its o= field, ". nodistro", is aptly's generic one.
origin deb.nodesource.com follow
# Tailscale carries the only path to the broker, and its postinst restarts
# tailscaled: its own held step, approved apart (as broker#67). Scoped by
# deploy/apt/tailscale.pref.
origin pkgs.tailscale.com follow
hold tailscale tailscale

# The scratch redis-server (localhost:6379, tests and smoke runs only) holds
# nothing to recover, so it gets no datastore line. Its packages stay the
# default `redis` held step: their postinst restarts it.

# --- owners ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The release is an extract with no git origin: its uv.lock is this repo's,
# updated through scripts/deploy.sh (the lock audit: docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).
owner /srv/processor/live self

records CannObserv/processor
